is too (observed on eka/adr:standard-version-1-4-corpus, whose accepted instance 1 and revision instance 2 disagreed until the transition was replayed), so the reset is not container-specific."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Cut EKA Standard 1.4 (additive minor) in eka-standard + eka-core, per the accepted decision eka/adr:standard-version-1-4-corpus:2. 1.3 stays exactly the shr- contract; the three post-1.3 normative commits (scope-aware container concurrency, validity horizon, provenance/capture envelope) and the exchange conformance corpus are classified as 1.4. Two corrections to the original sync set were required: eka-core/exchange/model.go and deserialize.go were missing from it (the EKA Version line is locked to exchange.SpecificationVersion by standardembed_test.go and cmd/version_test.go, so the bump forces both, and 1.3 packages would be refused at import without widening the accepted set); and CONTRIBUTING.md still claimed 'EKA Standard 1.1 is immutable' with a version list that stopped at 1.1. The eka-cli half of the sync set (vendored EKA copy, vendored.yaml re-pin, README standard axis) is deliberately deferred until eka-core is tagged, because eka-cli pins eka-core by released tag with no replace directive and no go.work. Tagging v1.3, v1.4 and the eka-core release is a human action.","tests":["eka-core: gofmt -l . clean; go vet ./... clean; go build ./... OK.","eka-core: go test ./... green — codegraph, compile, conformance, contexts, exchange, machine, metadata, plugin, runtime, store, sync, view, workspace.","Non-vacuity: replacing \"1.3\" with \"1.2\" in acceptedSpecificationVersions makes TestImportAcceptsEveryDeclaredSpecificationVersion fail with 'import refused: unsupported specification version \"1.3\" (found) — this importer validates against \"1.4\"'; restoring it returns the suite to green.","eka-standard: sha256sum -c conformance/exchange/SHA256SUMS all OK (corpus bytes untouched); grep for a stale current-version 1.3 leaves only historical matches (the CHANGELOG 1.3 section, the shr.md 1.3 attribution, and the versioning.md freeze line plus 1.3 bullet).","eka-cli: left unmodified (git status --porcelain empty); go test ./cmd/ ./... -run 'Version|Standard|Readme|Embed' green, which is the expected result while the eka-core pin still resolves to the 1.3-era release. Full go test ./... is blocked by the known-environmental hang eka/bug:test-suite-sqlite-fsync-hang."]}